  "summary": "New datasets, ensemble generators and pose-quality metrics address input diversity and evaluation for ML-driven structure-based ligand modeling.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is infrastructure for structure-based ligand modeling: curated data, conformational ensembles and evaluation criteria. DockBind pairs 18,332 quality-controlled docked complexes across 612 targets with affinity data, while Ternary-PDB curates 76,702 ternary structures alongside DiffTernary for molecular glue docking. PocketVec descriptors map 51,535 druggable human pockets to choose diverse Target 2035 targets. Ensemble generation appears in ANTIOCH-VS (ColabFold subsampling, AF2RAVE MD, docking, consensus ranking), Cadense for antibody Fv, and bAIes extended to six structure predictors for disordered proteins. CARVE adds glycan-specific pose scoring benchmarked on 1,974 complexes. The summaries report no head-to-head accuracy results, so novelty lies in resource construction, ensemble sourcing and evaluation design rather than demonstrated performance gains.",
